  "table_metadata": {
    "table_number": 1,
    "table_type": "main_soa",
    "table_title": "Schedule of Activities (SoA)",
    "table_purpose": "ISA NP02 (LY3526318, diabetic peripheral neuropathic pain) schedule: visits and procedures unique to the ISA, on top of the master CPMP and DPNP DSA CPMP(3) SoAs; V3-V7 and ED shared with the master, no follow-up visits added",
    "page_start": 11,
    "page_end": 12,
    "notes": "One label column (L=1); data columns at positions 2-7 (V3 -> 2, V4 -> 3, V5 -> 4, V6 -> 5, V7 -> 6, ED -> 7); the right-hand Notes column is not a schedule column. Typed main_soa: every participant randomised into this ISA passes through it in sequence. It is a delta schedule: the intro text says it shows only what is unique to the ISA, so the participant's full schedule is this table plus the master and DSA SoAs. The taxonomy has no type for that relation; it is recorded here and in g1. Three full-width section bands ('Scales, Questionnaires, and Outcome Measures', 'Clinical Laboratory Tests and Sample Collection', 'Participant Device') group the rows below them. Two redaction bars hide rows: the whole content of the 'Scales, Questionnaires, and Outcome Measures' group on p.11 (row position 11) and one row after 'PK sample' on p.12 (row position 21); both positions are unassigned and may each stand for more than one row."
  },
